1202
00:49:13,733 --> 00:49:16,933
of about -243 degrees
centigrade.

1203
00:49:17,000 --> 00:49:18,800
Uh, what was
the middle part again?

1204
00:49:18,867 --> 00:49:20,000
...by all that cold.

1205
00:49:20,067 --> 00:49:22,233
Well, professor newton
explained it this way:

1206
00:49:22,300 --> 00:49:24,300
- Heat can affect light waves...
- Blah-blah blah-blah

1207
00:49:24,367 --> 00:49:26,900
blah-blah-blah, that
are images, blah-blah-blah.

1208
00:49:26,967 --> 00:49:28,067
...can be seen by
the human eye.

1209
00:49:28,133 --> 00:49:30,267
Seen by blah-blah-blah,
blah-blah-blah mirage,

1210
00:49:30,333 --> 00:49:32,733
- blah-blah-blah blah-blah.
- Sure, I've seen them
on the sahara.

1211
00:49:32,800 --> 00:49:35,433
- Now intense cold can
have the opposite effect.
- Blah-blah cold blah-blah.

1212
00:49:35,500 --> 00:49:37,800
Blot out images that are
actually there.

1213
00:49:37,867 --> 00:49:40,067
I'm sorry,
I wasn't listening.

1214
00:49:40,133 --> 00:49:42,433
The rays sent out by
the terrifically cold light

1215
00:49:42,500 --> 00:49:44,733
will make the orbit jet
invisible.

1216
00:49:44,800 --> 00:49:47,267
Well, how can we fly
a ship we can't see?

1217
00:49:47,333 --> 00:49:49,867
The cold light
will surround the ship.

1218
00:49:49,933 --> 00:49:51,333
- [Scoffs] You idiot.
- We'll be able to see

1219
00:49:51,400 --> 00:49:53,000
everything normally
here in the cabins,

1220
00:49:53,067 --> 00:49:55,300
but no one will be
able to see us.

1221
00:49:55,367 --> 00:49:57,867
Well, if that can't get us
through any defense barrier,

1222
00:49:57,933 --> 00:49:59,267
nothing can.

1223
00:49:59,333 --> 00:50:00,733
Oh, just one point, winky.

1224
00:50:00,800 --> 00:50:02,600
- Shut up.
- We have to fight time.

1225
00:50:02,667 --> 00:50:04,900
We don't know how long
the cold lamp will operate,

1226
00:50:04,967 --> 00:50:06,900
so stand by
to switch it off, huh?

1227
00:50:06,967 --> 00:50:08,267
- Right, sir.
- Okay.

1228
00:50:15,367 --> 00:50:18,500
Hey, it's a universal film.

1229
00:50:18,567 --> 00:50:20,167
We're entering praa's
gravity field.

1230
00:50:20,233 --> 00:50:21,900
Switch it on, winky.

1231
00:50:21,967 --> 00:50:23,200
Okay.

1232
00:50:23,267 --> 00:50:25,167
- [Beeping]
- There, you see?
I did it, rocky.

1233
00:50:25,233 --> 00:50:26,533
I did it, I switched it on,
how did I do?

1234
00:50:26,600 --> 00:50:27,833
Did I do well?
I switched it on, I did it.

1235
00:50:27,900 --> 00:50:29,700
I did it. Did you see that?
I switched it on.

1236
00:50:29,767 --> 00:50:31,300
I can do it,
I can do it, and I did it.

1237
00:50:36,633 --> 00:50:38,800
- Cool.
- How do you know if
the ship's invisible?

1238
00:50:38,867 --> 00:50:40,833
Will I feel invisible?

1239
00:50:40,900 --> 00:50:42,167
But if something hits us,

1240
00:50:42,233 --> 00:50:44,600
we'll know the cold light
didn't work.

1241
00:50:44,667 --> 00:50:46,567
[Chuckles] That's
finding out the hard way.

1242
00:50:46,633 --> 00:50:48,200
You don't know the half
of it, little guy.

1243
00:50:48,267 --> 00:50:51,200
Boy, that's a rugged place.

1244
00:50:51,267 --> 00:50:54,200
- It's a van gogh.
- Van gaah.

1245
00:50:54,267 --> 00:50:55,667
Activate the gyro.

1246
00:50:55,733 --> 00:50:58,400
No, it's pronounced "ee-ro".

1247
00:50:58,467 --> 00:51:00,467
- Activated, sir.
- Secure for landing.

1248
00:51:00,533 --> 00:51:03,000
Please put your seats in their
locked, upright position.

1249
00:51:03,067 --> 00:51:05,333
But even if we can spot
a place in that rocky terrain

1250
00:51:05,400 --> 00:51:06,933
the orbit jet won't
stand on its tail.

1251
00:51:07,000 --> 00:51:08,567
- Don't start with me, winky.
- We're going to go

1252
00:51:08,633 --> 00:51:10,933
right into one of
their landing platforms.

1253
00:51:12,567 --> 00:51:14,400
Well, somebody's
gonna be surprised.

1254
00:51:14,467 --> 00:51:16,400
- [Goofy chuckle]
- I hope it isn't us.

1255
00:51:16,467 --> 00:51:17,567
D'oh!

1256
00:51:17,633 --> 00:51:20,300
You hear an invisible
ship just now?

1257
00:51:20,367 --> 00:51:21,567
Did they have
a signal for a landing?

1258
00:51:21,633 --> 00:51:24,333
Who could possibly
land on praa?

1259
00:51:24,400 --> 00:51:26,033
- Markov! Markov!
- Polo. Polo!

1260
00:51:26,100 --> 00:51:28,767
- Markov here.
- Who's making a landing?

1261
00:51:28,833 --> 00:51:31,333
Nothing's coming into
the landing platforms.

1262
00:51:31,400 --> 00:51:33,667
- Are you blind?
- Yes, sir, why do you ask?

1263
00:51:33,733 --> 00:51:35,000
Let's have a look, doc.

1264
00:51:36,400 --> 00:51:38,333
Sounds like a blimp.

1265
00:51:38,400 --> 00:51:39,933
[Beeping]

1266
00:51:40,000 --> 00:51:41,533
Keep
the visiograph on, winky.

1267
00:51:41,600 --> 00:51:42,867
You'll have to cover me.

1268
00:51:42,933 --> 00:51:44,633
If they start anything,
blast 'em.

1269
00:51:44,700 --> 00:51:46,633
I'll keep my
trigger finger ready.

1270
00:51:46,700 --> 00:51:48,400
You'll be able to
see me materialize

1271
00:51:48,467 --> 00:51:50,067
out of the ship's
invisibility blanket.

1272
00:51:50,133 --> 00:51:51,467
- I'll be buck naked.
- Boy, they're gonna be

1273
00:51:51,533 --> 00:51:53,200
even more surprised
than they are now.

1274
00:51:53,267 --> 00:51:56,100
Underneath those clothes
he's as smooth as a ken doll.

1275
00:51:56,167 --> 00:51:57,133
Right.

1276
00:51:59,867 --> 00:52:01,933
Oh, good,
now I can screw off.

1277
00:52:03,433 --> 00:52:05,733
The lavish new orchestra.

1278
00:52:05,800 --> 00:52:08,333
You could see no spaceship
has landed here.

1279
00:52:08,400 --> 00:52:11,267
It must have landed,
we heard the rockets.

1280
00:52:11,333 --> 00:52:12,733
Maybe we're all blind.

1281
00:52:12,800 --> 00:52:14,267
What do you think, doc?
You heard it.

1282
00:52:14,333 --> 00:52:16,133
I don't want to get involved.

1283
00:52:16,200 --> 00:52:18,533
I don't know,
it's fantastic.

1284
00:52:18,600 --> 00:52:20,900
[Beeping]

1285
00:52:22,333 --> 00:52:24,733
We're being paid to know
about these things, vanko.

1286
00:52:24,800 --> 00:52:26,600
Did a spaceship land
or didn't it?

1287
00:52:26,667 --> 00:52:30,033
- This thing is all beyond--
- [stammering] Uh,
sort of, I think.

1288
00:52:30,100 --> 00:52:31,467
You're gonna have
to keep up to date, doc...

1289
00:52:31,533 --> 00:52:33,067
- Um, maybe.
- Or you'll be dropped
back to earth

1290
00:52:33,133 --> 00:52:34,833
and wind up on
the exile planet.

1291
00:52:34,900 --> 00:52:37,633
Look,
there is your answer.

1292
00:52:37,700 --> 00:52:39,700
Hi, I'm your answer.

1293
00:52:39,767 --> 00:52:41,633
You expecting someone,
rinkman?

1294
00:52:41,700 --> 00:52:43,667
Nobody expects
the spanish inquisition!

1295
00:52:43,733 --> 00:52:46,800
You have discovered the light
vibration of invisibility.

1296
00:52:46,867 --> 00:52:49,700
It's friendly of you to bring
this new discovery to us.

1297
00:52:49,767 --> 00:52:52,467
He's got yummy icing
on his collar. Mmm!

1298
00:52:52,533 --> 00:52:54,233
I'm here with a warning.

1299
00:52:54,300 --> 00:52:57,133
Don't eat refrozen
ice cream.

1300
00:52:58,533 --> 00:53:00,700
There's the orbit jet,
take my word for it.

1301
00:53:00,767 --> 00:53:02,467
There's a gun on it
ready to blast you

1302
00:53:02,533 --> 00:53:04,100
if you make one false move.

1303
00:53:04,167 --> 00:53:07,267
- I like pancakes-- huh?
- I'll make it brief, rinkman.

1304
00:53:07,333 --> 00:53:10,067
Stop pirating the spaceships
of the united worlds,

1305
00:53:10,133 --> 00:53:12,333
or praa will be
blown out of existence.

1306
00:53:13,767 --> 00:53:16,033
That's big talk, rocky.

1307
00:53:16,100 --> 00:53:17,433
Mannix, no!

1308
00:53:17,500 --> 00:53:20,500
[Humming "mannix"
fight music]

1309
00:53:20,567 --> 00:53:22,367
Uh, winky, winky!

1310
00:53:22,433 --> 00:53:24,500
Oh, for crying out loud,
winky, I could use
a little help!

1311
00:53:24,567 --> 00:53:26,767
Help here, winky--
oh, winky!

1312
00:53:26,833 --> 00:53:29,033
Hey, wink--
[Groaning] Winky.

1313
00:53:30,667 --> 00:53:31,600
Winky?

1314
00:53:31,667 --> 00:53:32,900
I didn't think
the orbit jet

1315
00:53:32,967 --> 00:53:34,433
would fire on you
to get out.

1316
00:53:34,500 --> 00:53:36,733
He's got some
smooth pants on.

1317
00:53:36,800 --> 00:53:38,033
We'll take that chance.

1318
00:53:38,100 --> 00:53:40,033
Get him to the caves.

1319
00:53:40,100 --> 00:53:42,367
♪ For he's a jolly
good fellow ♪

1320
00:53:42,433 --> 00:53:44,000
♪ for he's
a jolly good fellow ♪

1321
00:53:44,067 --> 00:53:45,667
♪ for he's a jolly
good fellow... ♪

1322
00:53:45,733 --> 00:53:47,900
Oh, I know this is
coming up in my review.

1323
00:53:47,967 --> 00:53:50,033
[Groans]

1324
00:53:50,100 --> 00:53:51,500
You know, they really
didn't think through

1325
00:53:51,567 --> 00:53:53,600
the invasion of this planet
too well, did they?

1326
00:53:55,367 --> 00:53:57,167
- Cleolanta...
- Yes?

1327
00:53:57,233 --> 00:53:58,967
This is rinkman
on praa...

1328
00:53:59,033 --> 00:54:00,333
I'm under
your desk, actually.

1329
00:54:00,400 --> 00:54:02,033
Proceed with your report.

1330
00:54:02,100 --> 00:54:04,233
There's been a slight
change in our plans...

1331
00:54:04,300 --> 00:54:06,100
He's holding a bottle
of pierre cardin.

1332
00:54:06,167 --> 00:54:07,500
Hmm, and
his knee's on fire.

1333
00:54:07,567 --> 00:54:09,300
Why wasn't it
reported earlier?

1334
00:54:09,367 --> 00:54:11,100
Because I didn't
discover the change

1335
00:54:11,167 --> 00:54:14,000
- until rocky jones
landed on praa.
- [Coughing]

1336
00:54:14,067 --> 00:54:15,633
- Thank you.
- That's impossible.

1337
00:54:15,700 --> 00:54:18,333
No spaceship can get through
the defense barrier.

1338
00:54:18,400 --> 00:54:20,933
Rocky jones has
discovered a new trick.

1339
00:54:21,000 --> 00:54:22,300
He's here.

1340
00:54:22,367 --> 00:54:24,467
- What is he up to?
- Well, put him on.

1341
00:54:24,533 --> 00:54:26,733
Nothing much, as long
as I have him locked up

1342
00:54:26,800 --> 00:54:28,467
in one of the caves.

1343
00:54:28,533 --> 00:54:29,833
Keep him under guard.

1344
00:54:29,900 --> 00:54:32,400
You'll get further orders.
Out.

1345
00:54:32,467 --> 00:54:35,300
Mmm, let's see, I can wear
a camisole and a blazer.

1346
00:54:35,367 --> 00:54:36,833
No, that wouldn't
be right either.

1347
00:54:36,900 --> 00:54:39,267
- Uh...
- Um, hello.

1348
00:54:39,333 --> 00:54:40,767
No, hi. Hi.

1349
00:54:40,833 --> 00:54:42,400
I'm mylanta--
no, no.

1350
00:54:42,467 --> 00:54:43,633
Mr. Jones, I presume.

1351
00:54:43,700 --> 00:54:45,400
- No, how about--
- well, atlasan?

1352
00:54:45,467 --> 00:54:47,567
Yes, exclamation?

1353
00:54:47,633 --> 00:54:50,100
...to handle the execution
of rinkman and dr. Vanko.

1354
00:54:50,167 --> 00:54:52,200
- Rosencrantz and guildenstern.
- Cancel your orders.

1355
00:54:52,267 --> 00:54:53,667
But cleolanta,
that was your command.

1356
00:54:53,733 --> 00:54:56,333
- I went to a lot of trouble.
- I said cancel your orders.

1357
00:54:56,400 --> 00:54:58,200
What's the matter,
did they redeem themselves?

1358
00:54:58,267 --> 00:54:59,900
- For valuable prizes?
- I will go to praa

1359
00:54:59,967 --> 00:55:01,667
and decide if they
are to be pardoned.

1360
00:55:01,733 --> 00:55:03,100
Praa is a barren planet,

1361
00:55:03,167 --> 00:55:04,833
a land of rock
and granite mountains.

1362
00:55:04,900 --> 00:55:05,900
It's no place
for a woman.

1363
00:55:05,967 --> 00:55:06,933
Don't say barren to me.

1364
00:55:07,000 --> 00:55:08,533
Have my spaceship
made ready.

1365
00:55:08,600 --> 00:55:10,267
You will serve as pilot.

1366
00:55:10,333 --> 00:55:12,400
If that is
what you wish.

1367
00:55:12,467 --> 00:55:14,067
It is what I command.

1368
00:55:14,133 --> 00:55:16,300
And we know what kind
of weight that carries.

1369
00:55:18,400 --> 00:55:21,333
Oh, now my tummy's
upset. [Groans]

1370
00:55:21,400 --> 00:55:23,000
Oh, well,
I'll have to wear flats

1371
00:55:23,067 --> 00:55:24,600
if I'm gonna drive
a spaceship.

1372
00:55:24,667 --> 00:55:26,033
I'll probably get
his name wrong,

1373
00:55:26,100 --> 00:55:28,800
I'll call him sandy jones
or rusty jones.

1374
00:55:30,433 --> 00:55:31,633
Uh, you know what?

1375
00:55:31,700 --> 00:55:33,867
I should have known with
a guy like winky, you know?

1376
00:55:33,933 --> 00:55:36,100
Yeah, the guy's not even
good for ballast,

1377
00:55:36,167 --> 00:55:39,333
you know, looking at bobby
all funny, all...

1378
00:55:41,200 --> 00:55:42,267
Who wants gum anyway?

1379
00:55:42,333 --> 00:55:44,867
Oh, I love to
do that to myself.

1380
00:55:44,933 --> 00:55:46,867
Good thing they didn't
frisk him.

1381
00:55:46,933 --> 00:55:48,267
Winky?

1382
00:55:48,333 --> 00:55:50,100
Winky, am I
getting through?

1383
00:55:50,167 --> 00:55:52,367
You're coming in clear,
rocky.

1384
00:55:52,433 --> 00:55:54,700
I'm being held in a cave
in one of the mountains.

1385
00:55:54,767 --> 00:55:56,300
- I'll find it.
- [Beeping]

1386
00:55:56,367 --> 00:55:58,333
- I can't find it.
- I don't know how much
cold light we have left.

1387
00:55:58,400 --> 00:56:00,067
You are not to leave
the orbit jet.

1388
00:56:00,133 --> 00:56:01,667
I'll have to find
a way to get clear,

1389
00:56:01,733 --> 00:56:04,567
so keep the ship ready
for blastoff at any time.

1390
00:56:04,633 --> 00:56:07,767
Will do, but I feel like
a lunkhead just sitting here.

1391
00:56:07,833 --> 00:56:10,067
- Hold that thought, winky.
- Your job is to keep
the orbit jet invisible

1392
00:56:10,133 --> 00:56:12,833
just as long as
the cold light holds out.

1393
00:56:12,900 --> 00:56:14,167
- [Footsteps]
- Stand by.

1394
00:56:17,200 --> 00:56:18,667
Oh, hi, you must be rocky.

1395
00:56:18,733 --> 00:56:20,733
I'm supposed to take
your dinner order.

1396
00:56:22,100 --> 00:56:24,300
Rodin's "the thinker."

1397
00:56:24,367 --> 00:56:25,533
Two of them.

1398
00:56:25,600 --> 00:56:28,000
Rocky, suppose
we make a deal.

1399
00:56:28,067 --> 00:56:30,633
I'll give you $50 if you have
a hard-boiled egg in your purse.

1400
00:56:30,700 --> 00:56:33,600
You've got something good in
that secret of invisibility.

1401
00:56:33,667 --> 00:56:36,100
- Ralph ellison wants you.
- I think so.

1402
00:56:36,167 --> 00:56:38,233
I could get you
off praa alive...

1403
00:56:38,300 --> 00:56:40,267
- Praa...
- ...In exchange
for that secret.

1404
00:56:40,333 --> 00:56:43,467
You're wasting your time.

1405
00:56:43,533 --> 00:56:45,967
I'll put it this way:
Come in with me.

1406
00:56:46,033 --> 00:56:48,100
Join me, rocky,
we can rule the world.

1407
00:56:48,167 --> 00:56:51,067
You mean
as a space pirate?

1408
00:56:51,133 --> 00:56:53,633
- It pays off.
- Plus benefits.

1409
00:56:53,700 --> 00:56:54,967
Working out of
an invisible spaceship,

1410
00:56:55,033 --> 00:56:57,267
we'd have the solar system
by the tail.

1411
00:56:57,333 --> 00:56:58,900
Oh, great-- huh?

1412
00:56:58,967 --> 00:57:01,167
How about the people
you're taking orders from?

1413
00:57:01,233 --> 00:57:02,800
We won't be needing them.

1414
00:57:02,867 --> 00:57:05,100
- We can brush them off.
- Like dandruff.

1415
00:57:05,167 --> 00:57:07,067
Yes, but I don't know
who you're working for.

1416
00:57:07,133 --> 00:57:09,600
- You'd like to know...
- Winky, quit eavesdropping.

1417
00:57:09,667 --> 00:57:11,200
Get off the line!

1418
00:57:11,267 --> 00:57:12,500
[Rocky]
All right.

1419
00:57:12,567 --> 00:57:14,767
Well, rocky, is it a deal,

1420
00:57:14,833 --> 00:57:17,033
or do you rot it out
in this cave?

1421
00:57:17,100 --> 00:57:19,500
- Oh, that's the option?
- Mmm.

1422
00:57:21,733 --> 00:57:23,133
What'll it be, rocky?

1423
00:57:23,200 --> 00:57:24,800
Uh, I'll take
the surf and turf.

1424
00:57:24,867 --> 00:57:26,900
- I'm on vacation.
- Keep him covered, winky.

1425
00:57:26,967 --> 00:57:28,900
[Winky]
I got him covered, rocky.

1426
00:57:28,967 --> 00:57:31,233
You let a guy named winky
fool you?

1427
00:57:35,567 --> 00:57:36,500
Ooh!

1428
00:57:41,800 --> 00:57:43,133
Wendy, honey,

1429
00:57:43,200 --> 00:57:45,433
I think you hurt me
real bad.

1430
00:57:45,500 --> 00:57:48,033
Oh, uh, hi, my gun,
and, uh-- oh.

1431
00:57:48,100 --> 00:57:49,033
Huh?

1432
00:57:55,200 --> 00:57:56,600
[Imitates popeye]
What a revoltin' development.

1433
00:57:56,667 --> 00:57:58,800
Like a house of ill repute.
[Chuckles]

1434
00:57:58,867 --> 00:58:00,900
Hey, he moved
the entire cave wall.

1435
00:58:00,967 --> 00:58:01,900
Wow.

1436
00:58:03,567 --> 00:58:06,100
Come in. Come in!

